WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.600
In a world where nobody makes mistakes, there
might never be a need for superheroes.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.630
But in the real world nobody is perfect—including
the men and women who made the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:12.630
Universe.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:17.679
From The Avengers to X-Men, the folks behind
our favorite superhero movies are just as

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:19.869
human as the rest of us.

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:24.599
Here are a few mistakes you might have needed
super-vision to spot.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.710
Deadpool: Strange selfies

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:30.460
Deadpool's plans don't often go exactly as
he's intended—

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.939
"I forgot my ammo bag!"

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:33.210
"Should we turn back?"

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.180
"Nope, no time, I got this."

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.200
"Nine, ten, eleven, twelve bullets...or bust.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.300
Right here!"

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.150
-and apparently, neither do his selfies.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.850
During one of the fleeting happy moments in
the pre-super life of Wade Wilson, he takes

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.220
a cuddly photo with his lady.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:55.850
But when we see the actual Polaroid, both
the poses and the smiles are completely different.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.560
And it’s not the only time Deadpool’s
picture makes a sudden change...

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.820
Deadpool: The evolving self-portrait

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:09.060
During Deadpool's elaborate opening sequence,
we see a tattered, burning sketch that shows

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.929
our anti-hero using swords to decapitate a
nameless bad guy.

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:18.830
But when Deadpool creates the crayon self-portrait
later, he's using guns and the rest of the

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.150
doodle has changed.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.650
Napoleon Dynamite wouldn’t have made that
mistake!

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.410
Gosh!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.030
"Freaking idiot!"

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.219
Iron Man: Pepper's high-tech headset

00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:35.490
Tony Stark may be a billionaire playboy with
next-level technology, but even he doesn't

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.819
have invisible Bluetooth headsets.

00:01:37.819 --> 00:01:41.850
However, his assistant Pepper apparently does.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.529
After a quick cut away in Iron Man, the wireless
headset she's wearing during a phone call

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:52.049
disappears faster than Terrence Howard disappeared
from the cast of Iron Man 2.

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:53.949
Owww.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.940
"Next time baby"

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.109
The Amazing Spider-Man 2: The amazing backpack

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:04.409
Peter Parker obviously has a lot of stuff
to deal with, and can't be expected to know

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:07.429
what's going on with his accessories at all
times.

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:13.290
After just barely making it to Gwen Stacy's
graduation ceremony in The Amazing Spider-Man

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.910
2, his backpack repeatedly jumps from one
shoulder to both.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:22.360
With great power comes… well, lousy continuity.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.280
Ant-Man: Gun fever

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:29.990
One of the many upsides to being Ant-Man is
that you're able to control swarms of ants

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.200
with your mind.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.080
That comes in particularly handy when the
villainous Darren Cross holds a gun to the

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.060
head of Ant-Man and an army of ants jam the
gun's firing hammer.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:46.390
However, the type of pistol Cross is holding
throughout the scene doesn't have the external,

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.660
revolver-type hammer that's shown in the close-up.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.420
But let’s hear it for those noble ants anyway.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.000
Gambit's receding facial hair

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.410
There's no shortage of hairy men in Wolverine's
world, but Gambit takes it to the extreme

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.920
in X-Men Origins: Wolverine.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.380
When he encounters Wolverine in a bar, he's
got a scruffy mustache and beard.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.850
But after knocking Wolverine through a wall,
he's suddenly far more clean-shaven, making

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.330
it clear the scenes were shot on different
days.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.320
Spider-Man: Don't turn around

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.400
Sometimes the science behind Spider-Man's
web-slinging is a little iffy, but it's not

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.430
Spidey who breaks the laws of physics here.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.750
During a scene in Spider-Man in which large
chunks of a building are seen about to fall

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.450
on a lovely couple, we see the pair as they
run screaming towards the camera.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:41.440
But just a split-second later when Spider-Man
is about to pull them to safety, they're instantly

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.260
facing the other way…and not in much of
a hurry.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.250
Captain America: The Winter Soldier: Uh, where
are we now?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:54.910
For a movie about top secret military operatives
and ultra-advanced technology, there's a pretty

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:59.450
loose approach to geography in Captain America:
The Winter Soldier.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.620
The filmmakers post the location SHIELD HQ
onscreen.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:10.440
Although the latitude seems correct, the longitude
is listed as "south" when it should be "west."

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.010
Avengers: Age of Ultron: She's a witch!

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:19.320
Although this mistake might seem minor, it's
incredibly jarring to see it play out in real

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.320
time.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.941
As the Scarlet Witch talks to Captain America
in a scene from Avengers: Age of Ultron, she's

00:04:24.941 --> 00:04:27.930
got her head tilted to the left side of the
screen.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:32.300
But in the next shot from further back, she's
tilting her head the other way.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.150
Wait, what movie was this again?

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.150
Thanks for watching!

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:39.100
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.690
And leave us a comment to let us know your
favorite Marvel mistakes...

